### Module 6: Schema Conversion

Extracted fields from pattern matching are mapped into the unified event schema. This normalization step ensures that logs from different vendors are represented consistently.

#### Field Mapping Examples

| Extracted Placeholder | Schema Field | Normalization |
|-----------------------|--------------|---------------|
| `PORT_NAME` | `interface_id` | Normalize port naming conventions |
| `IP_ADDRESS` | `ip` | Validate and standardize format |
| `VLAN_ID` | `vlan` | Convert to integer |
| `MAC_ADDRESS` | `client_mac` | Normalize to colon-separated lowercase |
| `PEER_IP` | `bgp_peer_ip` | Validate as IPv4/IPv6 |
| `STATE` (up/down/online/offline) | `subtype` | Map to canonical state name |

#### Severity Normalization

| Vendor-Specific | Normalized |
|-----------------|------------|
| `emerg`, `alert` | `critical` |
| `crit` | `critical` |
| `err` | `error` |
| `warn` | `warning` |
| `notice` | `notice` |
| `info`, `debug` | `info` |

