## 11. Constraints and Considerations

| Constraint | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| **Causality is inferred, not proven** | The system uses heuristic and statistical methods to infer causality from temporal and contextual signals. Results should be validated by domain experts. |
| **Log completeness** | Analysis quality depends on the completeness of input logs. Missing logs from critical devices may lead to incomplete causal chains. |
| **Timestamp accuracy** | Clock skew correction improves accuracy but cannot fully compensate for severely unsynchronized devices. |
| **Scalability bounds** | While designed for sub-quadratic performance, extremely large incident windows (>100,000 events) may require parameter tuning. |
| **LLM dependency** | Natural language summarization quality depends on LLM availability and capability. Deterministic fallback ensures baseline functionality. |
| **Vendor coverage** | Initial support focuses on HPE/Aruba AOS-CX with extensible architecture for additional vendors. |
